          ":question/worked-solution": "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries to the left and to the right of ${a}_{12}=-1$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary column operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -4 & 10 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 9\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}: &={C}_{1}+2{C}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 & 4 \\\\ -5 & -4 & 10 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 9\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{3}: &={C}_{3}+4{C}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & -4 & -6 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 9\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary column operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+2{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+4{C}_{2}.$"
